{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>East of the Garden of Eden.</b> At the east of the Garden of Eden, outside the Garden." "<b>The cherubim.</b> Angels of destruction." "<b>The flame of the sword that turns.</b> And it has a flame to intimidate him from entering the Garden again. The Targum renders לַהַט as שְׁנַן — as in ״שָׁלַף שְׁנָנָא״; and in לַעַז לא״מא. And there are midrashic aggadot, but I come only for its plain sense."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {2 "The la'az לא״מא is Old French lamer (la mer), 'the blade/edge'; the Aramaic שְׁנָנָא means 'tooth/blade-edge'."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:28.888331280Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}